HTML <form> tag is used to create forms to take user inputs and information, much like the google forms of present time. 
It allows us to create labels, input fields, text area, buttons, checkboxes, radio buttons, dropdown menu etc. 

The uploaded example shows a form which has some lables for name, email, password. It also has radiobuttons, checkboxes and dropdown menu for taking differnet inputs.
We have used a little CSS as well to style the form instead of creating a raw HTML page.

